1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
This time, the technique class will talk about how to deal with hair blocking.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:18,000
When combing, if it is a style similar to a belt that covers the hair belt, then there will be a phenomenon of hair passing through the belt.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
And in the place of the seam, it also needs to have the effect of the hair being pressed by the sewing line.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
In this issue, I will talk about the processing techniques here.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
First of all, we choose the fixing needle tool.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,000
In the 3D window, empty selection, this step is to find the part of the belt covering the clothing.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Then when we add the fixing needle, you can see the marks added by the fixing needle on the 2D board.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Then the gap in the middle is the part of the belt covering.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
We can choose our basic line tool and draw the basic line on it.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Draw the range of our blocking.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
It is convenient for us to fill in the blanks later.

12
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Then when we are drawing, press the Ctrl key and the left-click button will appear.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Then we can draw the curve line.

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
After adding, we can come to the print mode.

15
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Then here we find the fabric of the jacket.

16
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Then we can pour out the fabric of our jacket here.

17
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Then here is the basic line that only needs to be displayed.

18
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Because the hair has no texture, you can choose the fabric texture directly to display the whole version in pure color.

19
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Then check the information, this side does not need to be selected.

20
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Then click Save.

21
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Then next, we open our picture in PS.

22
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,000
We can see that the gap in the middle is the part of the belt covering.

23
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
We can choose this part.

24
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Then fill it in.

25
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
We can add a layer.

26
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Then fill it in black.

27
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
We will make it a dense default picture.

28
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
There will be no hair in the black area.

29
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
There will be hair in the white area.

30
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
All kinds of layers will be displayed in one layer.

31
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:33,199
Then there will beefile in the top layer.

32
00:02:33,199 --> 00:02:36,000
And we press the Ctrl key to start a new layer.

33
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,919
Look for one layer here.

34
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,400
All layers were mostly black.

35
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:45,000
If we select this layer.

36
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
We can see here that the color is white.

37
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
We can use this layer is with white.

38
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
And we can select a layer.

39
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
All are black.

